Rule 1 (input tensor x must be of a supported numeric type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 4) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must have non-zero dimensions if its rank is greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor cannot be of boolean, unsigned integer, string, or dtype type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 5 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 7 (input tensor must have a supported numerical data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∃i ∈ [1, 4] : dtype_(v_1) = i ∨ ∃j ∈ [6, 10] : dtype_(v_1) = j
>>
Rule 8 (first two dimensions of a multidimensional tensor must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 9 (input tensor should have a rank of at most eight)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 8
